SYNTHESIS
  Raw separation is not the right carrier variable: rows with large gaps
  can still have very low exact relation height, e.g. offsets (30,60).
  The cap-budget ratios remain small in this bank, but they organize by
  relation-height and arithmetic phase more naturally than by raw gap.
  This supports the HYP-2717 proof split: finite-ledger low-height exact
  relations first, then a top-character Fourier tail for high-height rows.
